e then attached in the Settings\nSend\nFeedback report .\nThis a known problem and it has nothing to do\nwith the app . Usually the car radio is in a\ntemporary pairing mode and when you\ndisconnect it requires for the phone to pair\nagain and prompts for the PIN . On the car radio\nyou need to register the phone as a permanent\nand authorized connection . Please , consult the\nmanual . Another option\nnot very nice though\nis to use Tasker to input the PIN you need to\nGoogle this app .\nPIN For Each Connect", "children": [2], "label": 0, "human_label": -1}, {"id": 8, "class": "Text", "height": 11, "width": 58, "position": {"column_min": 19, "row_min": 578, "column_max": 77, "row_max": 589}, "text_content": "Donation", "label": 0, "human_label": -1}, {"id": 9, "class": "Text", "height": 12, "width": 87, "position": {"column_min": 18, "row_min": 597, "column_max": 105, "row_max": 609}, "text_content": "Donation Link", "label": 0, "human_label": -1}, {"id": 10, "class": "Text", "height": 21, "width": 5, "position": {"column_min": 402, "row_min": 41, "column_max": 407, "row_max": 62}, "text_content": "\u2012\u2012\u2012", "label": 0, "human_label": -1}], "img_shape": [768, 432, 3]}